Here's a single self-contained Python function that opens an image file, attempts OCR using Tesseract via pytesseract, converts/normalizes the text encoding to a clean Unicode string, and — if OCR fails or returns nothing — falls back to extracting image comments and EXIF user comments (decoding them robustly). It uses Pillow (PIL), pytesseract and chardet (all open-source).

